e_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the bug\r\n\r\nIn SA1.3.x, querying an alias of an alias of a mapped class yielded a SELECT against only one table, whereas in 1.4.x, querying an alias of an alias of a mapped class yields a SELECT against a comma join of a table with itself. \r\n\r\nHow do I reproduce the SA 1.3.x behavior in SA 1.4.x? \r\n\r\n### To Reproduce\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport sqlalchemy as sa\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import orm\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.declarative import declarative_base\r\n\r\n\r\nBase = declarative_base()\r\n\r\nclass User(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = 'user'\r\n    id = sa.Column('user_id', sa.Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    name = sa.Column('user_name', sa.String(50))\r\n\r\na1 = orm.aliased(User)\r\na2 = orm.aliased(a1)\r\n\r\ne = create_engine('postgresql://', echo=True)\r\ns = orm.Session(e)\r\n\r\nprint(s.query(a2))\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### Error\r\n\r\nIn SA 1.3.x, the SQL rendered is:\r\n\r\n```sql\r\nSELECT user_1.user_id AS user_1_user_id, user_1.user_name AS user_1_user_name\r\nFROM \"user\" AS user_1\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn SA 1.4.x, the SQL rendered is (note the comma join):\r\n\r\n```sql\r\nSELECT user_1.user_id AS user_1_user_id, user_1.user_name AS user_1_user_name\r\nFROM \"user\" AS user_1, \"user\" AS user_2\r\n```\r\n\r\nHow do I produce the 1.3.x result in 1.4.x, assuming I am only given `a2`? \r\n\r\n### Versions\r\n\r\n- OS: OSX\r\n- Python: 3.8.2\r\n- SQLAlchemy: 1.3.24 and 1.4.29\r\n- Database: postgres\r\n- DBAPI (eg: psycopg, cx_oracle, mysqlclient): psycopg\r\n\r\n\r\n### Additional context\r\n\r\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.